  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the town of Livonia, in the county of Livingston, to sell and convey the Jack Evans Community Center to the Little Lakes Community Association, Inc. for reasonable consideration",
    "basePrintNo": "S6387",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6387-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6387\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to authorize the town of Livonia, in the\ncounty of Livingston, to sell and convey the Jack Evans Community\nCenter to the Little Lakes Community Association, Inc. for reasonable\nconsideration\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nAuthorizes the town of Livonia, in the county of Livingston, to convey\nthe Jack Evans Community Center to the Little Lakes Community\nAssociation, Inc. for reasonable consideration.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Establishes legislative findings.\n\nSection 2. Provides definitions.\n\nSection 3. Provides that the local legislative body may by a\nresolution adopted by a two-thirds vote of its members, approve the\nsale of and convey title to the facility to the Little Lakes\nCommunity, Association, Inc., in exchange for what they shall\ndetermine to be reasonable consideration, and upon such terms as they\nmay find to be reasonable and in the best interests of the community.\nThis section also provides that such sale for reasonable consideration\nshall not be deemed an impermissible gift of local assets and/or\nproperty as is prohibited by section one of article VIII of the state\nconstitution, and that such sale for such reasonable consideration,\nshall be further deemed to be a sale for the fair market value of the\nfacility.\n\nSection 4. Provides that the legislation shall take effect\nimmediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Town of Livonia in Livingston County has been working to\nfacilitate transfer of the Jack Evans Community Center to Little Lakes\nCommunity Association, Inc. (\"Little Lakes\"), a 501 C (3), not for\nprofit organization for use as a community center, with secondary\nrental space that will support the primary community center use.\nUnfortunately, Little Lakes does not yet have the capital resources\nnecessary to pay fair market value for the property, as required by\nArticle VIII, section 1 of the New York State Constitution.\n\nThe property is currently in need of significant repairs and ongoing\nmaintenance to ensure that it does not fall into complete disrepair.\nThe Town does not feel that many of these repairs can wait for a\nprotracted time to allow Little Lakes to raise adequate capital to\naddress those repairs, along with all of the other financial burdens\nassociated with owning such a property. By way of example, the 25,000\n+/- square foot building uses approximately $20,000.00 worth of\nheating fuel each year. While Little Lakes is immediately prepared to\nundertake all utility and maintenance costs they cannot also come up\nwith funds to pay fair market value for the actual purchase of the\nproperty.\n\nThe Town has requested this legislation because it believes that\nLittle Lakes would be the ideal steward for this important and\nhistorical local structure. Unfortunately, because of the various\nconstraints that apply to a Town, Livonia has not been able to\noptimize the use of the facility. The mounting annual expenditures\nhave become difficult to justify and practically impossible to cover\nwithout significant impact to the tax rate.\n\nIt is in the best interests of the residents of the community for the\nTown of Livonia and the Little Lakes Community Association, Inc., to\nbe able to negotiate and complete a transaction through which the Town\nof Livonia will be able to sell or lease the real property,\nimprovements, and any personal property formerly known as and used for\nthe Jack Evans Community Center to the Little Lakes Community\nAssociation, Inc.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
